1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:01,700
You know,

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,567
when I was a kid, I was a really picky eater.

3
00:00:07,933 --> 00:00:14,267
- Yeah, I figured.
- But lately, everything tastes good to me.

4
00:00:15,733 --> 00:00:27,233
- It's probably thanks to you, Midori.
- Hard to buy that from a guy picking out the onions.

5
00:00:33,067 --> 00:00:34,633
Except raw onions.

6
00:00:38,033 --> 00:00:43,233
Well, the fact that he can't eat raw onions... is nothing new to me.

7
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:51,600
Hey! Who studies on the way to school?
Watch where you're walking!

8
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:56,933
Midterms are next week, you know? A strong start is everything, whether it's studying or anything el

9
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:01,133
- Midori, you're so cool!
- It's nothing special!

10
00:01:03,367 --> 00:01:09,233
Phew, thank goodness!
I dodged a failing grade.

11
00:01:11,033 --> 00:01:13,733
Midori? What's wrong?

12
00:01:15,833 --> 00:01:20,867
Huh? You're not first?
So close.

13
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:25,100
Ao Hayama

14
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:28,567
Oh! The results are up!

15
00:01:29,767 --> 00:01:33,833
-  Whoa, Ao You're number one!
- Oh, I see.

16
00:01:33,833 --> 00:01:35,333
Oh! Arisa!

17
00:01:36,367 --> 00:01:37,600
How'd you do?

18
00:01:45,933 --> 00:01:50,133
That's how I met Ao Hayama.

19
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:59,633
♪ Opening theme: "Crush on You" – ONE N' ONLY ♪

20
00:01:59,633 --> 00:02:07,733
♪

21
00:02:07,733 --> 00:02:10,933
♪

22
00:02:11,467 --> 00:02:15,300
♪

23
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:19,733
♪

24
00:02:19,733 --> 00:02:24,667
♪

25
00:02:24,667 --> 00:02:27,133
♪

26
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:33,067
♪

27
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:41,233
All right, for the last event, how about a relay between Class 1 and Class 3?

28
00:02:41,467 --> 00:02:41,967
Yeah!

29
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:44,733
Talk it over and decide among yourselves!

30
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:45,800
Okay!

31
00:02:47,433 --> 00:02:49,167
A relay sounds fun!

32
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:51,800
Let's do it!
Now we're talking!

33
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:53,067
Come on, let's do it!

34
00:02:53,367 --> 00:02:54,300
Are we doing it or not? You in?

35
00:02:54,567 --> 00:02:55,067
- Nah, I'm out

36
00:02:58,167 --> 00:03:00,133
Ao's our runner – it's settled!

37
00:03:00,667 --> 00:03:01,400
Huh? Me?

38
00:03:01,733 --> 00:03:03,867
Well, you're fast, aren't you?

39
00:03:03,867 --> 00:03:06,133
Am I?

40
00:03:07,167 --> 00:03:09,133
Me, Yoshida, Takase, and Okui.

41
00:03:09,133 --> 00:03:10,767
That's the whole track club!

42
00:03:10,767 --> 00:03:11,600
Is that even okay?

43
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:14,267
We can't lose to Class 1,
no matter what.

44
00:03:14,267 --> 00:03:17,033
- What, is this revenge for the test?

45
00:03:17,367 --> 00:03:18,867
I can't wait until finals.

46
00:03:18,867 --> 00:03:21,833
This one's in the bag.

47
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:24,567
I'll go win this!

48
00:03:27,133 --> 00:03:29,933
On your marks.

49
00:03:30,867 --> 00:03:32,367
Get set.

50
00:03:35,133 --> 00:03:37,067
Go!

51
00:03:37,067 --> 00:03:39,067
Go, for it!

52
00:03:39,067 --> 00:03:47,033
- Wow, Class 3 really is fast.
- Come on, Class 1!

53
00:03:51,033 --> 00:03:56,033
Oh no!  Ao, Come on, hang in there!

54
00:04:11,567 --> 00:04:12,733
Thank you.

55
00:04:56,733 --> 00:04:58,733
- Amazing! As expected of Onion Baby.
- Thanks.

56
00:04:58,733 --> 00:05:00,600
Winning like that is really something, huh?

57
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,833
Onion baby?

58
00:05:01,833 --> 00:05:03,833
- You guys were incredible!

59
00:05:03,833 --> 00:05:05,833
No doubt about it.

60
00:05:09,833 --> 00:05:11,833
- Thank you, thank you!
- You were so cool!

61
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:14,000
Yamamura!

62
00:05:14,533 --> 00:05:15,500
That was close.

63
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:18,700
Seriously, Isn't it cheating for that Hayama guy
to be fast at running, too?

64
00:05:18,933 --> 00:05:20,933
I was so sure we'd win.

65
00:05:20,933 --> 00:05:22,200
what a shame.

66
00:05:28,567 --> 00:05:29,233
I'm sorry.

67
00:05:36,467 --> 00:05:37,967
After all my big talk,

68
00:05:38,567 --> 00:05:39,533
I'm the one who got passed.

69
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:42,567
I dragged you all into this,

70
00:05:43,533 --> 00:05:44,667
and made you feel bad.

71
00:05:46,333 --> 00:05:48,000
I'm really sorry.

72
00:05:51,867 --> 00:05:52,600
Well,

73
00:05:53,233 --> 00:05:55,967
it made us realize
we hadn't practiced enough,

74
00:05:55,967 --> 00:05:56,800
so it was actually a good thing.

75
00:05:57,433 --> 00:05:57,933
Yeah, exactly.

76
00:05:58,367 --> 00:06:00,533
Guess we really do have to train properly.

77
00:06:01,833 --> 00:06:03,667
I fumbled the handoff a bit too.

78
00:06:03,667 --> 00:06:06,267
It's not just your fault, Yamamura, so don't worry about it.

79
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:16,600
Thanks.

80
00:06:20,767 --> 00:06:22,800
Guess it all comes down to practice, right?

81
00:06:24,367 --> 00:06:25,867
How much practice do we need?

82
00:06:27,167 --> 00:06:27,733
A thousand reps!

83
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:29,600
A thousand?!

84
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:31,333
Seriously?!

85
00:06:36,767 --> 00:06:37,267
Oh.

86
00:06:39,767 --> 00:06:41,033
Onion baby.

87
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,000
Onion baby?

88
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:46,067
Oh, Hayama.

89
00:06:46,833 --> 00:06:47,333
That's what...

90
00:06:47,333 --> 00:06:49,200
they called him in P.E.

91
00:06:50,900 --> 00:06:52,000
What does that even mean?

92
00:06:52,833 --> 00:06:54,200
You're that curious?

93
00:06:56,167 --> 00:06:57,667
We've got a score to settle.

94
00:06:58,700 --> 00:06:59,667
Or rather,

95
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:03,000
I want to find his weak spot.

96
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,200
I like that about you, Midori.

97
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:11,233
Hey, hey, Hayama.

98
00:07:12,733 --> 00:07:13,233
Yeah?

99
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,167
what, you can't eat onions?

100
00:07:15,833 --> 00:07:16,567
Yoshida.

101
00:07:16,567 --> 00:07:19,600
Well, you're curious, aren't you, Midori?

102
00:07:32,233 --> 00:07:32,733
Yeah.

103
00:07:33,567 --> 00:07:34,633
I can't eat them.

104
00:07:34,633 --> 00:07:35,133
Oh.

105
00:07:40,333 --> 00:07:42,333
Are you allergic or something?

106
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:44,000
No.

107
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:46,167
So you just don't like them?

108
00:07:48,067 --> 00:07:48,567
Yeah.

109
00:07:50,900 --> 00:07:51,733
Raw ones are spicy,

110
00:07:52,433 --> 00:07:53,367
I can't stand them.

111
00:07:55,067 --> 00:07:56,467
You don't like spicy things?

112
00:07:57,633 --> 00:07:58,133
Yeah.

113
00:07:58,767 --> 00:07:59,867
I like sweet things better.

114
00:08:05,533 --> 00:08:06,033
I see.

115
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:08,933
Onion baby.

116
00:08:10,033 --> 00:08:10,533
Oh.

117
00:08:15,167 --> 00:08:15,833
Want some?

118
00:08:16,667 --> 00:08:17,700
No, I don't want any.

119
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:20,100
I wasn't asking because I wanted some.

120
00:08:20,567 --> 00:08:21,233
Oh, okay.

121
00:08:33,232 --> 00:08:35,100
So it's Midori.

122
00:08:37,933 --> 00:08:38,433
Huh?

123
00:08:39,667 --> 00:08:40,167
Your name.

124
00:08:41,033 --> 00:08:42,832
I thought it was the same name as mine.

125
00:08:44,667 --> 00:08:46,033
Ah, true.

126
00:08:46,533 --> 00:08:48,233
It can be read as Ao, too.

127
00:08:50,167 --> 00:08:51,667
I'm Ao, though.

128
00:08:55,967 --> 00:08:57,167
I'm glad it's Midori.

129
00:08:59,067 --> 00:09:00,867
If we had the same reading,

130
00:09:00,867 --> 00:09:02,767
it'd be confusing.

131
00:09:09,567 --> 00:09:10,467
Whatever

132
00:09:10,967 --> 00:09:13,167
Hayama won't ever use my name anyway.

133
00:09:23,667 --> 00:09:24,233
He was kind of

134
00:09:24,233 --> 00:09:26,100
an interesting guy,

135
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:26,667
That Hayama.

136
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:28,133
Yeah.

137
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:30,700
So, are you going

138
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:31,900
to compete with him on the next test?

139
00:09:32,833 --> 00:09:33,367
Nah.

140
00:09:33,833 --> 00:09:35,133
I've lost the motivation.

141
00:09:35,133 --> 00:09:37,667
Oh, really?

142
00:09:39,867 --> 00:09:40,900
He turned out to be

143
00:09:42,267 --> 00:09:44,267
even more of a baby than I expected,

144
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:48,967
so I kind of—

145
00:09:49,667 --> 00:09:51,233
Did you think he's cute?

146
00:09:55,067 --> 00:09:55,900
I didn't.

147
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:59,800
My foot really hurts.

148
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:01,733
Hey,

149
00:10:01,733 --> 00:10:03,300
Yamamura,

150
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:04,600
you looked so cool in the relay.

151
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:05,667
Keep it up!

152
00:10:05,667 --> 00:10:07,000
Thanks.

153
00:10:12,533 --> 00:10:13,767
Midori— Kun

154
00:10:13,767 --> 00:10:15,400
I mean,

155
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:17,633
Yamamura - Kun

156
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:23,500
It's fine.

157
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:25,433
You can call me Midori.

158
00:10:26,367 --> 00:10:27,233
Huh?

159
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,300
Is that okay?

160
00:10:30,667 --> 00:10:31,667
Why are you so

161
00:10:31,667 --> 00:10:33,367
happy about it?

162
00:10:34,033 --> 00:10:34,533
Oh well, it's just...

163
00:10:35,267 --> 00:10:37,600
it feels like we've become friends,

164
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:39,600
and that makes me happy.

165
00:10:45,267 --> 00:10:46,167
what's wrong?

166
00:10:50,533 --> 00:10:51,033
No,

167
00:10:51,367 --> 00:10:52,367
it's nothing.

168
00:10:54,167 --> 00:10:54,833
Okay.

169
00:10:56,267 --> 00:10:56,767
Well then,

170
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:59,400
good luck at practice,

171
00:11:00,167 --> 00:11:01,000
Midori.

172
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:03,700
See you.

173
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:22,000
I like the girl in red.

174
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:22,500
Aw, really?

175
00:11:23,367 --> 00:11:24,700
I'd go with blue.

176
00:11:25,733 --> 00:11:26,533
What about you, Yoshida?

177
00:11:27,633 --> 00:11:28,133
Hm?

178
00:11:30,267 --> 00:11:31,167
Hmm...

179
00:11:31,167 --> 00:11:33,400
Going by looks, I'd say yellow.

180
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:35,700
Ah, she is good too.

181
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:36,900
What about you, Yamamura?

182
00:11:37,533 --> 00:11:38,033
Hm?

183
00:11:40,133 --> 00:11:40,633
Ah...

184
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,100
None of them.

185
00:11:43,967 --> 00:11:45,800
What, why?

186
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:48,367
There are cute ones and elegant ones.

187
00:11:48,367 --> 00:11:49,600
- None of them really clicks with me.

188
00:11:51,533 --> 00:11:52,300
I'm heading out first.

189
00:11:53,567 --> 00:11:55,900
Yamamura's standards are way too high.

190
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:03,100
I'm glad it's Midori.

191
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,600
If we had the same reading,

192
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,033
It'd be confusing

193
00:12:07,767 --> 00:12:10,033
it feels like we've gotten close,

194
00:12:10,033 --> 00:12:11,833
It makes me happy.

195
00:12:40,267 --> 00:12:41,467
Um, Midori.

196
00:12:42,267 --> 00:12:42,867
Hayama?

197
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:47,800
I heard Yoshida's out today.

198
00:12:50,067 --> 00:12:52,433
So, Um, if you don't mind...

199
00:12:54,233 --> 00:12:56,933
would you have lunch with me?

200
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:00,100
Hm?

201
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:03,633
Would you eat with me?

202
00:13:07,633 --> 00:13:08,133
Sure.

203
00:13:12,233 --> 00:13:13,033
Great!

204
00:13:14,667 --> 00:13:15,167
Then,

205
00:13:15,733 --> 00:13:17,067
I'll be waiting.

206
00:13:22,533 --> 00:13:23,033
Okay.

207
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:34,767
Hey,

208
00:13:35,233 --> 00:13:36,033
why me...?

209
00:14:01,433 --> 00:14:02,967
At it again?

210
00:14:03,967 --> 00:14:05,667
It's hard to pick them

211
00:14:05,667 --> 00:14:06,900
out of a sandwich!

212
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:08,500
Quit being stubborn.

213
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:10,000
Just give up and eat it.

214
00:14:12,167 --> 00:14:13,433
- Then do you want it, Midori-kun?

215
00:14:13,433 --> 00:14:14,800
- Nah, I'm good.

216
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:16,200
- But it'd be a waste!

217
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:17,933
Look who's talking.

218
00:14:17,933 --> 00:14:19,067
Here, take it.

219
00:14:19,067 --> 00:14:20,567
- No, I said I don't want it.

220
00:14:23,567 --> 00:14:24,067
Oh.

221
00:14:43,833 --> 00:14:44,567
This guy...

222
00:14:45,333 --> 00:14:47,433
really likes me, huh.

223
00:14:49,267 --> 00:14:50,633
If you're a picky eater,

224
00:14:50,633 --> 00:14:52,500
you won't grow big.

225
00:14:55,233 --> 00:14:56,567
I'm already big.

226
00:15:05,433 --> 00:15:06,133
Midori.

227
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:11,800
He can't hide how happy he is.

228
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,367
Such a baby.

229
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:15,500
Morning.

230
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:16,200
Morning.

231
00:15:17,967 --> 00:15:20,167
I thought today  was Sunday and overslept.

232
00:15:20,767 --> 00:15:22,067
I ran like crazy this morning.

233
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:24,233
Who does that

234
00:15:24,233 --> 00:15:25,233
on a Wednesday, right in the middle of the week?

235
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:28,333
I thought it was weird, too.

236
00:15:28,333 --> 00:15:29,333
I went back to sleep,

237
00:15:29,333 --> 00:15:30,767
and my mom dragged me out of bed.

238
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:34,367
I love sleeping, you know.

239
00:15:36,467 --> 00:15:36,967
So,

240
00:15:37,767 --> 00:15:39,233
that's why you've got bedhead.

241
00:15:39,933 --> 00:15:41,533
Huh? Oh, it is sticking up.

242
00:15:43,300 --> 00:15:43,833
Yeah, it is.

243
00:16:04,167 --> 00:16:04,967
Better yet,

244
00:16:05,433 --> 00:16:07,367
fix it before you go into class.

245
00:16:07,367 --> 00:16:08,233
See you.

246
00:16:13,633 --> 00:16:14,433
Midori.

247
00:16:15,267 --> 00:16:16,033
Did something happen?

248
00:16:18,333 --> 00:16:20,767
I can't be like that baby

249
00:16:20,767 --> 00:16:22,967
and just say I like what I like.

250
00:16:24,067 --> 00:16:24,933
It's nothing.

251
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:32,400
Still saying it was nothing,

252
00:16:34,167 --> 00:16:35,900
...until third year.

253
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:45,267
Midori.

254
00:16:45,267 --> 00:16:45,767
Hum?

255
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,167
can I come watch

256
00:16:50,933 --> 00:16:51,767
your last high school tournament?

257
00:16:55,033 --> 00:16:56,100
Sure, if you want

258
00:16:57,433 --> 00:16:59,233
but shouldn't you be studying?

259
00:17:00,567 --> 00:17:02,300
My exam prep is all set.

260
00:17:03,933 --> 00:17:04,666
More importantly,

261
00:17:05,633 --> 00:17:07,333
I'm more interested

262
00:17:07,333 --> 00:17:08,767
in seeing you shine in your last race.

263
00:17:13,333 --> 00:17:15,900
Well, do whatever you like.

264
00:17:16,967 --> 00:17:17,467
Okay.

265
00:17:18,433 --> 00:17:18,933
I will.

266
00:17:19,933 --> 00:17:21,166
Midori,

267
00:17:21,166 --> 00:17:23,433
let's go to practice.

268
00:17:24,267 --> 00:17:24,867
Oh.

269
00:17:27,467 --> 00:17:28,733
See you.

270
00:17:28,733 --> 00:17:29,233
Yeah.

271
00:17:41,167 --> 00:17:42,800
That Hayama...

272
00:17:43,533 --> 00:17:45,067
Don't you think he likes you,

273
00:17:45,367 --> 00:17:46,100
Midori-kun?

274
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:47,067
What?

275
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:48,767
I mean,

276
00:17:48,767 --> 00:17:51,267
he's practically overflowing

277
00:17:51,267 --> 00:17:52,867
with love for you.

278
00:17:52,867 --> 00:17:54,767
So cute.

279
00:17:57,367 --> 00:18:02,633
Don't say creepy things.

280
00:18:02,633 --> 00:18:03,133
Midori.

281
00:18:09,267 --> 00:18:10,533
Do you really mean that?

282
00:18:16,567 --> 00:18:18,167
The one who gets hurt by what you say

283
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:20,367
is yourself, isn't it?

284
00:18:36,167 --> 00:18:36,867
You're right.

285
00:18:39,933 --> 00:18:41,267
I shouldn't have

286
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:44,533
said something like that.

287
00:18:49,933 --> 00:18:51,833
You get it, huh?

288
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:53,700
Okay,

289
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:55,067
let's go, let's go.

290
00:18:55,067 --> 00:18:55,933
We'll be late.

291
00:19:13,967 --> 00:19:17,400
Midori-kun, once you're in college, will you forget about me?

292
00:19:18,467 --> 00:19:19,733
I won't forget.

293
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,167
What about you?

294
00:19:21,167 --> 00:19:22,733
You'll be helping at your grandma's
flower shop, right?

295
00:19:23,367 --> 00:19:25,000
You'll be so busy

296
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:26,133
you won't have time for me.

297
00:19:26,133 --> 00:19:28,033
Huh? Of course I will!

298
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:30,333
Besides,  Come visit the shop sometime.

299
00:19:30,333 --> 00:19:32,033
Grandma's waiting for you, too.

300
00:19:32,567 --> 00:19:35,200
Okay, okay. I'll come.

301
00:19:37,933 --> 00:19:39,300
Hey, Midori.

302
00:19:40,367 --> 00:19:41,167
How was it?

303
00:19:41,633 --> 00:19:42,533
High school life, I mean.

304
00:19:43,433 --> 00:19:44,233
What do you mean, how was it?

305
00:19:46,167 --> 00:19:47,900
Did you have any change of heart,

306
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:48,467
or anything?

307
00:19:50,933 --> 00:19:51,733
Hmm...

308
00:19:54,767 --> 00:19:55,500
Nope.

309
00:19:58,500 --> 00:19:59,767
Nothing at all.

310
00:20:02,533 --> 00:20:03,267
Nothing, really

311
00:20:04,533 --> 00:20:05,300
Hey, hey, hey!

312
00:20:06,267 --> 00:20:08,133
The track club's getting together after this.

313
00:20:08,133 --> 00:20:09,733
Let's sing till our voices give out! It's graduation day!

314
00:20:09,733 --> 00:20:11,500
Let's go sing like crazy!

315
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:13,667
And the former captain had better show up.
No skipping out

316
00:20:13,667 --> 00:20:15,233
Okay, okay, I'll come.

317
00:20:15,733 --> 00:20:17,200
Let's compete for the high score!

318
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:18,833
Oh, you're on!

319
00:20:18,833 --> 00:20:21,133
Of course I'm good!

320
00:20:21,833 --> 00:20:23,033
All right, Midori-kun,

321
00:20:23,033 --> 00:20:24,467
we're heading ahead.

322
00:20:24,467 --> 00:20:26,267
Race you there—ready, go!

323
00:20:59,167 --> 00:21:00,100
Midori.

324
00:21:04,567 --> 00:21:05,867
Congratulations on graduating.

325
00:21:13,733 --> 00:21:14,767
You know,

326
00:21:18,767 --> 00:21:20,233
because you were there, Midori,

327
00:21:20,233 --> 00:21:25,067
school was fun.

328
00:21:36,333 --> 00:21:37,867
Because of me?

329
00:21:42,367 --> 00:21:43,033
Yeah.

330
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:50,933
Really, Thank you.

331
00:22:03,633 --> 00:22:04,267
Well,

332
00:22:09,067 --> 00:22:10,200
see you.

333
00:22:25,833 --> 00:22:26,967
Hayama.

334
00:22:26,967 --> 00:22:27,467
Oh.

335
00:22:34,933 --> 00:22:35,900
Don't you have anything

336
00:22:38,867 --> 00:22:39,833
you want to say to me?

337
00:22:51,167 --> 00:22:51,833
This is

338
00:22:53,233 --> 00:22:54,967
the best I can do right now.

339
00:23:10,367 --> 00:23:11,667
That's so cool.

340
00:23:12,567 --> 00:23:13,600
Seriously.

341
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:15,400
Hayama,

342
00:23:15,400 --> 00:23:17,767
are you really okay graduating like this?

343
00:23:18,467 --> 00:23:20,133
Waking up in the morning,

344
00:23:20,133 --> 00:23:21,233
Midori's eyelashes...

345
00:23:22,267 --> 00:23:23,633
I wish I could see them.
